### Approvals flow + Automations — API smoke harness
#
# Walks the full client-approval loop against a live WordPress install. Use with
# the VS Code "REST Client" extension, JetBrains HTTP client, or translate to
# curl. Run top-to-bottom; later requests reuse values captured from earlier
# responses (token, setId).
#
# Prereqts on the target WP:
#   - Plugin active, DB upgraded to >= 1.14.0 (tables wp_pcm_automations,
#     wp_pcm_automation_logs; columns brands.clientEmail, approval_sets.clientEmail).
#   - A published page containing the [power_creatives] shortcode (for share links).
#   - Logged-in admin session OR an X-WP-Nonce for the authenticated calls.
#   - (For real email) a Brevo integration row (provider='brevo') + Settings
#     automations_from_email; (for real webhooks) Settings global_webhook_url
#     or a brand additionalContext.webhookUrl. Without these, dispatch is logged
#     as "skipped"/no-op — the flow still returns 2xx.

@base = http://powercreatives.local/wp-json/pcm/v1
@nonce = REPLACE_WITH_WP_REST_NONCE
@token = REPLACE_WITH_TOKEN_FROM_CREATE
@setId = REPLACE_WITH_ID_FROM_CREATE

### 1. Create an approval set (authenticated team action)
# Capture `token` and `id` from the response into @token / @setId above.
POST {{base}}/approvals/sets
X-WP-Nonce: {{nonce}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Smoke Test Set",
  "brandId": null,
  "projectId": null,
  "snapshot": {
    "brandName": "Acme",
    "media": [{ "id": "m1", "type": "image", "url": "https://example.com/a.png" }],
    "copy":  [{ "id": "c1", "headline": "Hello", "body": "Body" }]
  }
}

### 2. Share the set with a client by email (authenticated)
# Dispatches approval.set.shared → Brevo invite email (or logged "skipped").
POST {{base}}/approvals/sets/{{setId}}/share
X-WP-Nonce: {{nonce}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "client@example.com" }

### 3. Client opens the set by token (public, no auth)
GET {{base}}/approvals/sets/{{token}}

### 4. Client posts a comment on an asset (public)
# Dispatches approval.comment.created → team webhook. Returns the new comment
# with a server-generated UUID + status "New".
POST {{base}}/approvals/sets/{{token}}/comment
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assetId": "m1", "body": "Can we brighten this image?", "author": "Client" }

### 5. Team replies in the thread (authenticated)
# Dispatches approval.comment.team_reply → client email.
POST {{base}}/approvals/sets/{{setId}}/reply
X-WP-Nonce: {{nonce}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assetId": "m1", "body": "Done — brightened version attached." }

### 6. Client approves the first asset (public)
POST {{base}}/approvals/sets/{{token}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assetId": "m1", "approved": true }

### 7. Client approves the rest → set auto-advances to "launch"
# When every snapshot asset is approved, the response status becomes "launch"
# and approval.all_approved fires the team webhook exactly once (idempotent —
# re-running this request does NOT re-fire it).
POST {{base}}/approvals/sets/{{token}}/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{ "approveAll": true }

### 8. Verify final state (status should be "launch")
GET {{base}}/approvals/sets/{{token}}

### --- Automations module management (authenticated) ---

### 9. List automation rules
GET {{base}}/automations
X-WP-Nonce: {{nonce}}

### 10. Inspect the event/channel catalog
GET {{base}}/automations/events
X-WP-Nonce: {{nonce}}

### 11. Create an explicit webhook rule (overrides the default)
POST {{base}}/automations
X-WP-Nonce: {{nonce}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event": "approval.all_approved",
  "channel": "webhook",
  "config": { "url": "https://hooks.example.com/pcm", "secret": "shared-secret" }
}

### 12. Send a test webhook (blocks, returns the HTTP result)
POST {{base}}/automations/test
X-WP-Nonce: {{nonce}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "channel": "webhook", "config": { "url": "https://hooks.example.com/pcm" } }

### 13. Send a test email via Brevo
POST {{base}}/automations/test
X-WP-Nonce: {{nonce}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "channel": "email", "to": "you@example.com" }
